            <ArticleTitle>Sex differences in late behavioral response to subcutaneous formalin injection in mice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>185-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We investigated sex- or gender-dependent differences in nociception using the formalin test in mice. In addition to typical biphasic responses, a new, late phase (Phase 3) was observed. A local anesthetic QX-314 injected at the end of Phase 2 blocked Phase 3. Phase 3 in female mice was significantly greater than that in male mice regardless the stage of the estrus cycle.</AbstractText>
